  "behavioral_change": "pandas v_old 2.1.4 to v_new 2.2.0. SeriesGroupBy.aggregate with pd.Series.nunique on a category column (Categorical._groupby_op) produces a result with a different dtype; the sources record this as an upstream regression rather than an intentional change.",
  "downstream_effect": "A numeric deviation appears in an outer nested aggregation, far from the nunique output dtype that causes it; scored under the frozen test_patch.",
